==Old English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|ang|haldan}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|ang|gem-pro|*haldaną||to watch, look after}}. Cognate with {{cog|ofs|halda}} ({{cog|fy|hâlde}}), {{cog|osx|haldan}} ({{cog|nds|holen}}), {{cog|odt|haldan}} ({{cog|nl|houden}}), {{cog|goh|haltan}} ({{cog|de|halten}}), {{cog|non|halda}} ({{cog|sv|hålla}}, {{cog|da|holde}}), {{cog|got|𐌷𐌰𐌻𐌳𐌰𐌽}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈhæɑldɑn/|lang=ang}}

===Verb===
{{ang-verb}}

# {{lb|ang|West Saxon}} to keep watch over (cattle etc.)
# {{lb|ang|West Saxon}}to [[hold]] fast, to [[grasp]]
# {{lb|ang|West Saxon}} to [[contain]]
# {{lb|ang|West Saxon}} to [[possess]]
# {{lb|ang|West Saxon}} {{lb|ang|intransitive}} to maintain one’s position against an enemy

